.TH WIFI.CONF 5
.SH NAME
wifi.conf \- the Wi-Fi network to join
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B /etc/wifi.conf
.SH DESCRIPTION
The Wi-Fi server,
.BR wifid (4),
keeps the chosen network here and joins it again at every start.
It writes the file when root joins a network
.RB ( wifi (1),
or Settings on the desktop) and removes it when root forgets the network.
Mode 0600: root only, since it holds the passphrase in clear.
.PP
Two
.IB key = value
lines:
.TP
.BI ssid= NAME
the network's name, at most 32 bytes
.TP
.BI passphrase= WORDS
its WPA2 passphrase, at most 64 bytes; empty for an open network
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
ssid=home
passphrase=correct horse battery staple
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR wifi (1),
.BR wifid (4)
